\begin{abstract}
This paper presents a formal validation and proof framework for the multi-scale simulation architectures,
pipeline designs, and stress-testing protocols developed by C.~Matthew Blackwell. Validation is established
across three pillars: (i) cryptographic ingress and data integrity, (ii) relativistic and gravitational
trajectory convergence, and (iii) cosmological and morphological stability. Each pillar is supported by
explicit mathematical invariants, bounded error metrics, and reproducible test procedures suitable for
independent peer review and architectural verification.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}

The architectures under validation integrate:
